# ADLMS Frontend Design

Use this rule for UI, sidebar, navigation, dashboard, and Blade layout changes.

## UI Principles

- Operational users need speed, clarity, and predictable navigation.
- Do not show all menus at once when grouped navigation is better.
- Preserve role and permission gates.
- Keep active menu state stable.
- Prevent sidebar flicker/jump on page refresh.
- Make dashboards scannable and responsive.
- Avoid purely decorative UI that slows operators down.

## Known Layout Context

Canonical sidebar file:

- resources/views/layouts/sidebar.blade.php

Known shell/topbar:

- resources/views/layouts/navigation.blade.php

## Sidebar Rules

- Group menus by workflow.
- Keep permission checks around each group/item.
- Use stable route-name based active states.
- Avoid dead links like `#` unless intentionally a collapsed group toggle.
- Avoid duplicated navigation logic.
- Keep mobile behavior intact.

## Dashboard Rules

For Owner/Admin dashboard:

- show key operational metrics first
- highlight pending orders, production bottlenecks, QC rejects, delivery pending, low stock
- use branch filters where applicable
- never mix branch data unless user role is allowed to see all branches
